---
components: ["BumpChart"]
description: Bump chart shows how ranks change over several periods, as a line per series with its rank in every period.
---

<script>
  import { BumpChart } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";

  const WEEKS = ["W1", "W2", "W3", "W4", "W5", "W6"];
  const RANKS = {
    Ada: [1, 1, 2, 3, 3, 2],
    Bell: [2, 3, 3, 1, 1, 1],
    Cray: [3, 2, 1, 2, 4, 4],
    Dijkstra: [4, 4, 4, 4, 2, 3],
    Euler: [5, 5, 5, 5, 5, 5],
  };
  const standings = Object.entries(RANKS).flatMap(([team, ranks]) =>
    ranks.map((rank, i) => ({ week: WEEKS[i], team, rank })),
  );

  const MONTHS = ["Jan", "Feb", "Mar", "Apr"];
  const SIGNUPS = {
    Search: [820, 760, 910, 990],
    Referral: [640, 720, 700, 1020],
    Social: [450, 810, 560, 480],
    Paid: [700, 650, 580, 610],
  };
  const channels = Object.entries(SIGNUPS).flatMap(([channel, values]) =>
    values.map((signups, i) => ({ month: MONTHS[i], channel, signups })),
  );

  let selected = null;
</script>

`BumpChart` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

It is a [SlopeChart](/components/SlopeChart) for many periods, and for ranks rather than values: rank one runs along the top, and a line bumps down or up as its series loses or gains places. The rank is written in every dot, so the picture never rests on position alone. Every line is labeled at both ends, so there is no legend.

## Basic

Pass long `data` with `x` for the period, `rank` for the place, and `series` naming each line. Periods run in the order first seen; set `periods` to fix them.

<BumpChart data={standings} x="week" rank="rank" series="team" title="League standings by week" />

## Rank by value

Give `y` instead of `rank` to rank each period by its values, the largest first. The value is then in the tooltip and in the table.

<BumpChart data={channels} x="month" y="signups" series="channel" title="Signup channels ranked by month" />

## Selection and size

Bind `selected` or listen for `select`, whose detail carries every point of the line. `width`, `rowHeight`, and `labelWidth` set the geometry; `colors` fixes a series' color and `palette` picks another color group.

<BumpChart data={standings} x="week" rank="rank" series="team" bind:selected rowHeight={28} colors={{ Ada: "success" }} title="Pick a team" />

## Accessibility

The chart is a single tab stop. Down and Up walk the lines by their final rank, announcing each with its first and last rank and how far it moved. Enter or Space selects, Escape clears. The figure also holds a visually hidden table with the rank of every series in every period.
